# 高频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List03核心词汇

{{design}}{/dɪˈzaɪn/}{设计；构思}{The team designed a user-friendly interface.}}
{{despite}}{/dɪˈspaɪt/}{尽管；不管}{Despite the challenges, the project was completed on time.}}
{{detect}}{/dɪˈtekt/}{发现；探测}{The software can detect errors automatically.}}
{{determine}}{/dɪˈtɜːmɪn/}{决定；确定}{Your choices determine your future.}}
{{develop}}{/dɪˈveləp/}{发展；开发}{The company developed a new vaccine in record time.}}
{{devote}}{/dɪˈvəʊt/}{奉献；致力于}{She devoted her career to public health research.}}
{{dimension}}{/daɪˈmenʃn/}{维度；方面}{The problem has both social and economic dimensions.}}
{{discipline}}{/ˈdɪsɪplɪn/}{纪律；学科}{Self-discipline is essential for achieving long-term goals.}}
{{distinguish}}{/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ/}{区分；辨别}{It is important to distinguish between fact and opinion.}}
{{distribute}}{/dɪˈstrɪbjuːt/}{分配；分发}{The organization distributes aid to disaster-affected areas.}}
{{domestic}}{/dəˈmestɪk/}{国内的；家庭的}{Domestic policy focuses on healthcare and education.}}
{{dominate}}{/ˈdɒmɪneɪt/}{支配；占主导地位}{A few large companies dominate the market.}}
{{dramatic}}{/drəˈmætɪk/}{戏剧性的；显著的}{There has been a dramatic shift in public opinion.}}
{{economy}}{/ɪˈkɒnəmi/}{经济；节约}{The national economy grew by 3% last year.}}
{{eliminate}}{/ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt/}{消除；淘汰}{The goal is to eliminate poverty in the region.}}
{{emerge}}{/ɪˈmɜːdʒ/}{出现；浮现}{New trends are emerging in the technology sector.}}
{{emphasis}}{/ˈemfəsɪs/}{强调；重点}{The report places emphasis on sustainable development.}}
{{enable}}{/ɪˈneɪbl/}{使能够；使可能}{The new law enables citizens to access public records.}}
{{encounter}}{/ɪnˈkaʊntər/}{遭遇；邂逅}{Students encounter various challenges during their studies.}}
{{engage}}{/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ/}{从事；吸引}{The campaign aims to engage young voters.}}
{{enhance}}{/ɪnˈhɑːns/}{增强；提高}{Technology can enhance the learning experience.}}
{{enormous}}{/ɪˈnɔːməs/}{巨大的；庞大的}{The city has an enormous demand for affordable housing.}}
{{ensure}}{/ɪnˈʃʊər/}{确保；保证}{We must ensure that all students have equal access to education.}}
{{establish}}{/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/}{建立；设立}{The university was established in 1850.}}
{{estimate}}{/ˈestɪmeɪt/}{估计；估算}{Experts estimate that the project will cost $5 million.}}
{{evaluate}}{/ɪˈvæljueɪt/}{评估；评价}{Teachers evaluate student performance through various methods.}}
{{eventually}}{/ɪˈventʃuəli/}{最终；终于}{After much deliberation, she eventually agreed.}}
{{evidence}}{/ˈevɪdəns/}{证据；迹象}{There is compelling evidence to support this theory.}}
{{evolve}}{/ɪˈvɒlv/}{进化；发展}{The company has evolved into a global leader in tech.}}
{{exceed}}{/ɪkˈsiːd/}{超过；超出}{Demand has exceeded supply in recent months.}}
